  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0070_a2af1d2e089e.jpg\" style=\"height: 252px; width: 250px;\" /><br />Plates 1-2, 2-3, 3-4 and 4-5 form a total of four capacitors.<br /><br />The capacity of each capacitor is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br />From figure, it is clear that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math>"
